hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"470","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you bathe except with a person near him who does not look, while close to him and speaking to him."
"471","With the same chain, from al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not bathe in the open desert unless you see a screen; and if you do not find one, let one of you draw a line like a room, then mention Allah and bathe within it."
